  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader of my topic lists, I want the top bar without the refresh button and with the title pill centred in the free space between the account button and the trailing buttons, so that the bar is lighter (refresh is done by pulling the list, see the companion issue on pull to refresh). (Operator feedback, 2026-11-18, device screenshot of Favoris: account avatar, « Favoris » pill, then filter / refresh / « … » in a trailing group.)\n\n### Today (dev-swift)\n\n- The topic list's trailing toolbar group holds « Non lus / Tous » (Favoris only, #1058), « + » (category lists), the refresh button, and « … ».\n- The refresh button is legacy's `ToolbarRefreshIcon` (an `arrow.clockwise` that spins while loading, `Common.swift:393-404` @ 87fe0d1c), ported by #770 (`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListView.swift:86-110, 330-340`).\n- The list already refreshes on a pull (`.refreshable`, `TopicListView.swift:120`).\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Remove the refresh button from the topic lists' top bar: Favoris, Drapeaux, category lists and any list that shows it. The pull to refresh stays. The spinning-while-loading feedback moves to the pull's own indicator. This is a deliberate difference from legacy and #770: record it as a `gap-edit` in the ledger.\n2. Centre the title pill in the free space between the leading account button and the trailing group, without any custom layout trick. The navigation title (principal placement) is centred by the system. If the system centres it on the screen width rather than the free space, state that in the PR with a screenshot and keep the system behaviour, as the operator rule of #1070 requires: stay within Apple's behaviour. Removing one trailing button already narrows the gap.\n3. The other screens with a refresh button in the toolbar (Alertes Qualitaÿ, profile) are out of scope unless they share the same component. Check, and say which.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No refresh button in the topic lists' top bar. A test pins the toolbar items per list kind, and it fails on today's code.\n- [ ] Pull to refresh still works on every topic list.\n- [ ] Before/after screenshots (Favoris and a category list, light and dark), plus a device check on the next general review (#893).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
